I guess your suggestion is quite reasonable, and would be the logical
choice as the default answer. However, I have my doubts that the Dev Team
will actually change this. I have experience in this.

I once suggested changing the default value for rest_on_space to
NOrest_on_space in the example default.nh/.nethackrc file that is shipped
with the official distribution, because new players often get killed by
tapping the space bar once too often.

The Dev Team rejected that idea on the grounds of it changing the way that
file had been for a long time. The only thing they did was add the
following text:
  "Note: the rest_on_space in the next line may not be appropriate for a
   beginning NetHack player, since it could result in use of a turn
   unintentionally. If you're new to NetHack, comment it out. It is being
   left in to keep the sample config file the same as it was in past
   releases"
to that option in the file itself. Not very useful, I think, since not all
newbies will even realise the file is there.

Therefore, I think it's quite improbable that they will change something
that happens as often as getting the "eating" warning, if they're already
reluctant to change the options file (which you will probably change only
once).

> In other words, how many times have you hit 'n' to the "Stop eating"
> questions by mistake?  Or is it just me?  :)

It never happened to me, probably because of the reason above: I am used
to the current interface.

